# Galaxy S26: the other llama.cpp Gemma 4 prompt rows that ran with thinking on (budget-mode-rule, 2026-10-19), listed
# for a re-measure decision; a list, not a job file. The fix is the runner's (android/bench/run_cell.py: a Gemma 4 GGUF
# row hands its chat template enable_thinking = false; docs/dashboard-cells-v1.md "Android llama.cpp Gemma 4 thinking
# (2026-10-19)"); the page cells come first in matrices/dashboard-llama-thinkoff-android.cells (Pixel 8a) and
# matrices/dashboard-llama-thinkoff-s26-{e2b,e4b,side-e2b,side-e4b}.cells (S26). Every row below is byte-identical to its
# source line; each group runs by its source file's route:
#   - the side build's long-context-1024-gen256 rows (page cells llama.cpp-npu / llama.cpp-gpu; E2B measured 2026-10-08
#     with thinking on, E4B not measured): matrices/dashboard-npu-v1-android-s26.cells lines 29, 30, 39, 40. By hand,
#     as matrices/dashboard-npu-v1-android-s26-short.cells says (a 1K launch raised the battery up to 4.1 C, and the job
#     has no battery-temperature stop).
#   - the 2K ladder (long-context-2048-gen256 at context-tokens 2304 / 4096 / 8192, llama.cpp b8999 on 2026-09-20/21):
#     matrices/dashboard-longctx-v1-android-s26.cells lines 54-56, 76-78 (= dashboard-longctx-v1-android-s26-gemmae2b.cells
#     lines 29-31 and -gemmae4b.cells lines 29-31). Round mode, as that file's header says (ROUNDS=8 COOLDOWN=30
#     THERMAL_WAIT=600 BENCH_CPU_MASK=; long-context-2048-gen256 needs ROUNDS=N).
# Not listed: the protocol rows (dashboard-protocol1024-v1-android.cells, dashboard-npu-protocol1024-v1-android-s26*.cells)
# are native-benchmark-1024x256 = llama-bench, which has no prompt and no chat template (unchanged by the fix); the
# Gemma 4 rows of dashboard-longctx1024-v1-android-a.cells (line 29) and -b2.cells (line 24) are byte-identical to
# dashboard-text-v1-android-a.cells line 31 and -b2.cells line 19, the 1K rows of dashboard-llama-thinkoff-android.cells.
# The first row is the Android session anchor, byte-identical to matrices/dashboard-llama-b11721-android.cells line 20.

android llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF short-chat anchor=1 runs=3 file=Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf

